# What never reaches the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile only COPYs `pyproject.toml` and `image_gallery/`, so most of
# this is belt-and-braces — but the context is still uploaded to the daemon on
# every build, and an exclusion here is what stops a `COPY . .` added later from
# silently shipping the test suite. The image carries no test scaffolding at
# all, which is a guardrail the project states and `tests/e2e/conftest.py`
# relies on when it calls the fake's control API test-only.

# Version control and local tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.venv
venv
.vscode
.idea

# Python build and bytecode artifacts
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
dist
build
*.egg-info

# Everything to do with testing. `tests/` holds the suite, its fixtures, its
# fake upstream, its own compose stack, and its generated reports.
tests
.pytest_cache
.coverage
coverage.xml
htmlcov
.tox
.nox

# Runtime output that must be produced inside the image rather than copied in:
# collectstatic runs during the build, and the cache directory is a tmpfs mount
# at run time.
staticfiles
.gallery-cache

# Documentation and orchestration, none of which the application imports
docs
README.md
django_image_gallery_assignment.md
compose.yaml
Dockerfile
.dockerignore

# Local environment overrides
.env
*.local
